allTriangulations(Matrix) -- use topcom to generate all triangulations of a point or vector configuration
*********************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note allTriangulations: allTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp,
  * Usage: 
        allTriangulations A
        allTriangulations(A, Homogenize => true, Fine => true, RegularOnly => true)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Homogenize => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true
      * ConnectedToRegular => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value true
      * Fine => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false
      * RegularOnly => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

This function constructs all triangulations of the point set corresponding to
$A$ (or triangulation of the cone over $A$, if Homogenize => false is given.
With no optional arguments, the default is to construct all regular
triangulations.

This function is a wrapper for the topcom function *note
topcomAllTriangulations: (Topcom)topcomAllTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp,, and has
the same optional arguments as that function. This function returns a list of
Triangulation (missing documentation)'s.

A triangulation is a list of list of the indices of the maximal simplices in
the triangulation. (the index of the point corresponding to the $i$-th column
(starting at $0$) is simply $i$.

For example, the following point set is the smallest which has a non-regular
triangulation.

