Caveat
======

This function is written in the top level Macaulay2 language, and so is much
slower than *note allTriangulations: allTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp,, which
calls the topcom code written in C++.  On the other hand, one can give this
function a limit for the number of triangulations to generate, so can be used
to generate triangulations in the case when the number is too large to write
down all of them.

See also
========

  * *note allTriangulations: allTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp, -- use topcom to
    generate all triangulations of a point or vector configuration

Ways to use generateTriangulations:
===================================

  * "generateTriangulations(Matrix)"
  * generateTriangulations(Matrix,List) (missing documentation)
  * generateTriangulations(Triangulation) (missing documentation)

For the programmer
==================

The object *note generateTriangulations: generateTriangulations, is a *note
method function with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

